00:47:45.370 --> 00:47:46.730
but they're pretty straight forward,

1194
00:47:46.730 --> 00:47:50.210
positive prediction error, or a negative prediction error.

1195
00:47:50.210 --> 00:47:52.930
So, using cake as an example,

1196
00:47:52.930 --> 00:47:55.510
if we see a piece of chocolate cake,

1197
00:47:55.510 --> 00:47:58.007
and we haven't had it from a certain bakery before,

1198
00:47:58.007 --> 00:47:59.317
we expect it to have, you know,

1199
00:47:59.317 --> 00:48:01.180
like, "Oh, I like chocolate cake."

1200
00:48:01.180 --> 00:48:03.368
We expect it to have a certain reward value.

1201
00:48:03.368 --> 00:48:05.967
Then we eat it and we go, "Oh my goodness,

1202
00:48:05.967 --> 00:48:08.920
"this is the best chocolate cake I've ever had in my life."

1203
00:48:08.920 --> 00:48:11.160
And suddenly there's this positive prediction error,

1204
00:48:11.160 --> 00:48:13.790
because we predicted it to be of X reward,

1205
00:48:13.790 --> 00:48:15.880
and it was actually X plus a thousand, you know?

1206
00:48:15.880 --> 00:48:17.060
It was much more rewarding.

1207
00:48:17.060 --> 00:48:19.250
So, we're like, "Oh, I gotta remember that bakery."

1208
00:48:19.250 --> 00:48:22.470
And we learn to go back there for a good chocolate cake.

